<div class="kicker"><a href="/">Follow the Money</a> · Straw poll</div>
<h1>Build Your 2028 Dream <em>Ticket</em></h1>
<div class="standfirst">The 2028 race is already surfacing — earlier than anyone expected. Pick your President and Vice President from the names the polls and the movement are floating. Every card is sourced; nobody's here because we made them up.</div>
<div class="meta">{{ ticket2028.race }} · updated {{ ticket2028.updated }} &nbsp;·&nbsp; anonymous · no login</div>

<div class="ticket-slots" id="ticketSlots">
  <div class="slot" id="slot-pres"><span class="slot-role">President</span><span class="slot-name" id="pres-name">— pick one —</span></div>
  <div class="slot-x">+</div>
  <div class="slot" id="slot-vp"><span class="slot-role">Vice President</span><span class="slot-name" id="vp-name">— pick one —</span></div>
</div>
<div class="ticket-actions">
  <button class="start-btn" id="lockTicket" type="button" disabled onclick="lockTicket()">Lock in my ticket</button>
  <button class="start-btn again" id="shareTicket" type="button" onclick="shareTicket()" style="display:none">📤 Share my ticket</button>
  <button class="start-btn again" id="changeTicket" type="button" onclick="changeTicket()" style="display:none">↺ Change my ticket</button>
  <div class="ticket-share-row" id="ticketShareRow"></div>
  <div class="locked-note" id="lockedNote" style="display:none">✓ Ticket locked for this browser — one at a time; you can change it.</div>
</div>

<div class="cand-grid">
{%- for c in ticket2028.candidates %}
  <div class="cand" data-id="{{ c.id }}">
    <div class="cand-head"><span class="cand-name">{{ c.name }}{% if c.caveat %} <span class="cand-caveat" title="Has not committed to running">⚑</span>{% endif %}</span><span class="cand-lane">{{ c.lane }}</span></div>
    <ul class="cand-facts">
    {%- for f in c.facts %}
      <li>{{ f.text }} <a href="{{ f.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">— {{ f.label }} ↗</a></li>
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <div class="cand-pick">
      <button class="pick-btn pick-pres" type="button" onclick="pick('pres','{{ c.id }}')">★ President</button>
      <button class="pick-btn pick-vp" type="button" onclick="pick('vp','{{ c.id }}')">☆ VP</button>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="sourcing-note">These names are drawn from public polling and party/advocate chatter as of {{ ticket2028.updated }}. Every fact links to its source; a <span class="cand-caveat">⚑</span> marks candidates who haven't committed to running (Ossoff and Whitmer have said no). This is an <strong>unscientific straw poll</strong>, not an endorsement or a prediction — one ticket per browser, and like any open poll it measures enthusiasm, not electorates.</div>

<h2>How the country's building it</h2>
<div class="leaderboard" id="leaderboard"><p class="lb-empty">Loading the standings…</p></div>

<h2>The receipts</h2>
<p>Every figure above is public — polling and campaign-finance disclosures. Check them yourself:</p>
<div class="receipts"><ul>
{%- for c in ticket2028.candidates %}
  <li><span>{{ c.short }}</span><span class="receipt-srcs">
  {%- for f in c.facts %}
    <a href="{{ f.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ f.label }} ↗</a>
  {%- endfor %}
  </span></li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul></div>

<script>window.__TICKET = { {% for c in ticket2028.candidates %}"{{ c.id }}": "{{ c.short }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };</script>
<script src="/assets/dream-ticket.js"></script>
